### ===== RUN THESE 3 LOGINS FIRST (they save the tokens) =====

### 1. Login as CUSTOMER (Maria)
# @name customerLogin
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "maria.santos@gmail.com",
  "password": "Customer@123"
}

### 2. Login as STAFF (Marco)
# @name staffLogin
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marco.delosreyes@gmail.com",
  "password": "Staff@123"
}

### 3. Login as ADMIN (Giuz)
# @name adminLogin
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "giuz.montano@gmail.com",
  "password": "Admin@123"
}

### Saved tokens (filled in automatically from the 3 logins above)
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.token}}
@staffToken = {{staffLogin.response.body.token}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}


### ===== GUARD 1: protect (are you logged in?) =====

### 4. "Who am I?" with NO token (expect 401 "Please log in first")
GET http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me

### 5. "Who am I?" with a FAKE token (expect 401 invalid/expired)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi

### 6. "Who am I?" as the customer (expect 200, Maria Santos, no passwordHash)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ===== MY PROFILE =====

### 7. Update my phone + try to make myself admin (expect 200, role STILL customer)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "09179998888",
  "role": "admin"
}

### 8. Change my email to one that is already used (expect 409)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marco.delosreyes@gmail.com"
}

### 9. Change password with the WRONG current password (expect 400)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "WrongPass123",
  "newPassword": "Maria2026new"
}

### 10. Change password to a WEAK one (expect 400)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Customer@123",
  "newPassword": "short"
}

### 11. Change password correctly (expect 200)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Customer@123",
  "newPassword": "Maria2026new"
}

### 12. Login with the OLD password (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "maria.santos@gmail.com",
  "password": "Customer@123"
}

### 13. Login with the NEW password (expect 200)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "maria.santos@gmail.com",
  "password": "Maria2026new"
}


### ===== GUARD 2: allowRoles (is your role allowed?) =====

### 14. View ALL reservations with NO token (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations

### 15. View ALL reservations as CUSTOMER (expect 403 "You do not have permission")
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 16. View ALL reservations as STAFF (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### 17. CUSTOMER tries to confirm a reservation (expect 403)
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/r2/status
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Confirmed"
}

### 18. STAFF confirms the reservation (expect 200)
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/r2/status
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Confirmed"
}

### 19. CUSTOMER tries to edit a table (expect 403)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tables/t11
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "available"
}

### 20. ADMIN edits the table (expect 200)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tables/t11
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "available"
}


### ===== PUBLIC (no login needed) =====

### 21. View tables with no token (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/tables

### 22. Check availability with no token (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/availability?date=2026-10-12&time=19:00&guests=2
